                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Head Start is a lifeline for over 800,000 children, providing high-quality early education, health, and nutrition services. These programs rely on timely funding to cover essential expenses like employee pay, rent, and utilities. Without federal funding, many centers could be forced to close, leaving thousands of children and families without access to vital childcare and education.\n\nThat\u2019s why I joined @HouseDemocrats in demanding the Trump Administration immediately release these delayed Head Start funds. We must ensure these centers receive the support they need to stay open and continue giving children the foundation they need to thrive. Our children\u2019s futures depend on it.",
